Description: An operating system command is built or executed using untrusted input without neutralizing shell metacharacters.
Vulnerability indicators:
- User input concatenated or interpolated into a string passed to system/popen/os.system/subprocess
- subprocess with shell=True and arguments built from external data
- Unvalidated file names or parameters used as an argument of an executable
Safe patterns:
- Argument list without a shell (subprocess.run([...], shell=False)) or execv with a fixed argv
- Strict allowlist of permitted values before execution

